  "body": "## Result\n\nOne new exact package: `research/p112-matched-frame-copy-floor/`, on base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`.\n\nFor any finite masked P112 decoder over C with ordinary transpose, suppose every paid rank-one term has **equal F2 source/target support spans** and pairing-rank COPY cost at most four. Actual supports need not coincide or be tetrad-local. Arbitrary coefficients, cancellations and zero-cost corrections are allowed.\n\nThe package proves\n\n`n1 + 2 n2 + 4 n3 + 5 n4 >= 112`, hence **COPY >= 84**.\n\nIts rank-relaxation optimizer is uniquely 28 rank-three terms; this is **not a constructed COPY84 decoder**. The COPY moment is at least **21/16** of the incumbent eight rank-eight copies, for every `0 <= a < 1` at unchanged normalization. A common-span radical quotient and the characteristic-vector complement relation give the rank-four lifted capacity five, rather than the naive eight.\n\nThe fully charged optimistic retained-template ceiling is `[0.000736244670745, 0.000736244670746]`, below the unchanged five-percent target `0.00177455681454345`. Both local COPY mass and centre charge rise from 64 to 84; idle mass stays 1646. Every additional physical charge is waived only to make this rejection favorable. **No new kappa, supplier admission, physical frame contract, frontier change or positive construction-gate success is claimed.**\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- All 12,544 root/label/coordinate entries, including masked target `4I_112`.\n- All **452** nonsingular nonalternating symmetric F2 forms through dimension four; lifted rank capacities **1,2,4,5**.\n- Exact P112 witnesses attaining each per-term capacity, including distinct actual supports with the same label span.\n- Fraction row elimination plus independent odd-prime column rank corroboration.\n- Semantic controls for missing/wrong diagonal terms, wrong mask, arbitrary zero-cost correction and undercharged centre.\n- Explicit unmatched-span rank-two/lift-three and matched rank-five/lift-ten counterexamples showing why the scope restrictions matter.\n\n## Reproduction actually exercised\n\nOn **CPython 3.12.12**, Darwin arm64:\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -B research/p112-matched-frame-copy-floor/verify.py --write\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/p112-matched-frame-copy-floor/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/p112-matched-frame-copy-floor\n```\n\nDirect and registered replays passed:\n\n`PASS_P112_MATCHED_FRAME_COPY_FLOOR forms=452 entries=12544 capacities=1,2,4,5 COPY>=84 moment_ratio>=21/16 controls=7 no_new_kappa`\n\n`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/p112-matched-frame-copy-floor outcome=negative-result`\n\nThe coordinating parent independently reviewed the quantified proof and repeated the registered Python 3.12 replay before granting publication. This is not independent human review or a proof-assistant theorem. Native/hosted CI and the selected full cold replay were not run or claimed.\n\n## Selection, overlap and limits\n\nIndependent one-shot chooser seed **`5cee555544503585ad60b2631e790c0c`**; track **complex-mechanisms**; emitted and chosen card **complex-rank-shape-decoder**. Complete chooser JSON, exact source pins, TASK scope refinement and replay manifest are included.\n\nThis uses the card's allowed scoped support-alphabet lower bound, not its positive five-percent construction gate. It is distinct from #1909 (one-tetrad locality with arbitrary opposite support), #1923 (a finite Householder orbit of one symmetric witness), and #1633 (all-pairs outside-root-code ranks). Targeted cached/local searches and live predecessor head checks found no same-scope result; no literature-priority guarantee is implied.\n\nUnmatched support spans, COPY rank at least five, other punctures, nonseparate copy accounting and changed role/coverage interfaces remain outside the theorem. A high-rank mask fixture is not a decoder. README includes exact proof, physical limitations and concrete open next questions.\n\nCoordination: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1929#discussioncomment-18925923\n\nCredit DreamingOfClouds for PR717's masked decoder/COPY model, Mihir Srivastava for pinned geometry, themilkman216 for frame-pair predecessor results, Douglas Colkitt for the exact ceiling engine, and the selected supplier chain. Prepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra) assistance; Apache-2.0. All predecessor, frozen and selected files are unchanged.\n",
